WEBVTT

00:05.350 --> 00:07.284
Thank you for transporting me home.

00:07.719 --> 00:12.418
You are a terrific cab driver
and I hope some day to visit your country.

00:15.961 --> 00:17.724
Damn, where is that key?

00:17.896 --> 00:21.127
Here, key, key, key.

00:22.534 --> 00:23.762
Aha!

00:25.237 --> 00:27.762
Hello, key.

00:34.246 --> 00:35.736
Oh, no.

00:35.914 --> 00:37.939
Wrong house.

00:38.750 --> 00:40.684
I'm lost.

00:42.988 --> 00:44.512
Hello?

00:45.390 --> 00:47.756
Oh, hey, Alan. Come on in.

00:49.428 --> 00:50.895
Why don't you come in here?

00:51.296 --> 00:53.389
I can't. I lost my key.

00:55.567 --> 00:57.831
Dah!

01:02.140 --> 01:04.335
Had a few cocktails, did we?

01:04.643 --> 01:06.008
Me too.

01:06.311 --> 01:08.245
Listen, I need to ask you a favor.

01:08.413 --> 01:12.179
Your needs. Your needs.
What about my needs?

01:12.918 --> 01:15.352
Are you capable
of having a conversation?

01:15.520 --> 01:16.953
Capable?

01:17.122 --> 01:19.955
I just spent 20 minutes
discussing open-toed shoes...

01:20.125 --> 01:22.116
...with a fat man from Rangoon.

01:24.596 --> 01:26.928
He's a Rangoonian.

01:27.666 --> 01:30.601
- We'll talk in the morning.
- I wouldn't count on it.

01:31.036 --> 01:32.799
Go ahead, you talk, I'll cook.

01:33.105 --> 01:34.732
It's 11:30. What are you cooking?

01:34.906 --> 01:38.069
Good question. And I can give you
the answer in two words:

01:38.243 --> 01:41.212
My famous homemade chili.

01:41.613 --> 01:43.376
Since when do you make chili?

01:43.548 --> 01:46.142
There's a lot
you don't know about me, Alan.

01:49.121 --> 01:51.089
I am a man of many layers.

01:51.757 --> 01:54.317
- Strata, if you will.
- I see.

01:54.493 --> 01:56.654
A thin crust, magma...

01:56.828 --> 01:59.296
...and a chewy nougat center.

02:00.198 --> 02:04.100
Great. Anyway, tomorrow I have to go
to the DMv to get my license renewed.

02:04.503 --> 02:08.530
Ah, cars.
Where would we be without cars?

02:08.707 --> 02:10.971
And how would we get there?

02:12.277 --> 02:15.144
Run, run, you're free.

02:15.981 --> 02:17.881
Well, listen, the thing is...

02:18.050 --> 02:21.451
...I can't take Jake,
because he's got a book report to do.

02:21.987 --> 02:24.012
I love Jake.

02:24.189 --> 02:26.953
Well, that's good.
But will you help him with his report?

02:27.125 --> 02:29.320
I would like nothing better.

02:29.494 --> 02:31.462
- You want chili?
- No, I'm good.

02:31.630 --> 02:33.962
But just so we're clear, you'll help Jake?

02:34.966 --> 02:36.263
I love Jake.

02:37.169 --> 02:39.000
- Charlie, it's very important...
- Relax.

02:39.171 --> 02:42.538
I'll take Jake to the DMv
to get his license.

02:44.342 --> 02:45.934
Book report.

02:47.846 --> 02:49.871
Beans.

03:01.526 --> 03:03.187
Oh, no.

03:03.695 --> 03:06.425
Charlie's blackout chili.

03:08.467 --> 03:09.593
It's delicious.

03:09.768 --> 03:11.360
No argument there.

03:11.536 --> 03:13.026
Why is it called blackout chili?

03:13.505 --> 03:15.234
Well, sweetheart...

03:15.407 --> 03:19.036
...sometimes when people drink,
they do things they wouldn't normally do.

03:19.411 --> 03:21.572
Me, I like to walk into a biker bar...

03:21.747 --> 03:23.874
...and take a swing
at the biggest chick there.

03:25.784 --> 03:29.049
Your uncle Charlie, on the other hand,
makes chili.

03:29.721 --> 03:31.154
But what's the blackout part?

03:31.556 --> 03:32.989
Oh, jeez, Jake.

03:33.158 --> 03:36.059
How many times have I told you
not to crap up my kitchen?

03:36.228 --> 03:38.355
But I'm not the one who...

03:38.530 --> 03:40.293
oh.

03:40.832 --> 03:44.734
Still, it beats waking up to find pool chalk
between your fanny cheeks.

03:48.340 --> 03:49.568
So where's your father?

03:49.741 --> 03:53.233
He went to the DMv. He said you promised
to help me with my book report.

03:53.411 --> 03:55.345
Really? That doesn't sound like me.

03:56.181 --> 03:58.172
I didn't think so, but that's what he said.

03:58.583 --> 04:00.175
- Whers it due?
- Monday.

04:00.352 --> 04:02.980
- Okay. Today's Saturday?
- Yeah.

04:03.555 --> 04:05.079
We got plenty of time.

04:05.257 --> 04:07.691
Yeah, but my dad always says
if I do my work early...

04:07.859 --> 04:09.588
...I have the weekend to have fun.

04:09.961 --> 04:12.589
That makes no sense whatsoever.

04:12.764 --> 04:14.459
That's what I said.

04:15.734 --> 04:16.928
Let me ask you something.

04:17.102 --> 04:18.763
- Do you wanna do it now?
- No.

04:18.937 --> 04:21.371
Then trust your instincts.

04:21.540 --> 04:22.973
Here's what you do.

04:23.141 --> 04:24.768
You go out, have a good time.

04:24.943 --> 04:27.138
Let the report percolate
in your subconscious.

04:27.946 --> 04:32.383
Then, as the deadline approaches
and that flop-sweat panic hits...

04:32.551 --> 04:36.510
...those pages will come shooting
out of you like lunch from a supermodel.

04:37.956 --> 04:39.287
Well, I do like to percolate.

04:39.457 --> 04:41.186
Attaboy.

04:41.927 --> 04:43.622
And what are you doing today?

04:43.995 --> 04:46.691
I've gotta write a new jingle
for a credit-card company...

04:46.865 --> 04:49.595
...and they're expecting it on Monday.

04:49.768 --> 04:51.599
So I'm going to the track.

04:52.671 --> 04:56.698
&lt;i>WoMAN
Now serving Number 38 at Window D.&lt;/i>

04:58.577 --> 05:00.636
I got 42.

05:01.179 --> 05:03.147
I made an appointment.

05:03.548 --> 05:05.209
Good for you.

05:08.820 --> 05:10.481
What's your number?

05:11.857 --> 05:14.485
- I'm 97.
- Mm. Ouch.

05:14.659 --> 05:16.524
You're gonna be here forever.

05:18.930 --> 05:20.454
Yeah.

05:22.601 --> 05:24.535
Oh, hey, you know what?

05:24.736 --> 05:27.068
I'm probably not even gonna need
this PowerBar.

05:27.239 --> 05:28.729
You want it?

05:28.974 --> 05:30.305
Thanks.

05:30.475 --> 05:32.375
You're very kind.

05:33.979 --> 05:36.311
Next time, plan ahead.

05:36.781 --> 05:37.941
Will do.

05:38.116 --> 05:40.710
- You gotta know how to work the system...
- Again...

05:40.886 --> 05:42.251
...thanks.

05:45.056 --> 05:46.455
Okay, I'm leaving.

05:46.625 --> 05:47.649
Bye.

05:47.826 --> 05:49.487
If you need anything, ask Berta.

05:49.661 --> 05:51.094
- Okay.
- She won't give it...

05:51.263 --> 05:53.288
...but she enjoys being asked.

05:53.598 --> 05:55.327
All right.

06:01.539 --> 06:04.508
- Turn that off, you're coming with me.
- Really? To the track?

06:04.676 --> 06:07.338
It's gotta be better for you than Tv.

06:09.414 --> 06:12.349
- Are we gonna gamble?
- No, suckers gamble.

06:12.517 --> 06:15.577
We're gonna analyze statistics
with proven scientific principles...

06:15.754 --> 06:18.780
...and make wagers
based on the resulting data.

06:21.192 --> 06:22.716
I think I'd rather watch Tv.

06:23.261 --> 06:24.990
Come on. Come on.

06:25.830 --> 06:28.765
&lt;i>WoMAN
Now serving Number 39 at Window A.&lt;/i>

06:29.301 --> 06:33.135
It appears my time on your planet
is almost over. Ha-ha-ha!

06:33.305 --> 06:34.863
"Ha-ha-ha!"

06:35.040 --> 06:37.235
Excuse me, are you done
with your paper?

06:37.409 --> 06:39.172
Oh, sure. Here.

06:39.511 --> 06:41.138
Thank you.

06:41.313 --> 06:44.180
I didn't even have a chance
to finish the jumble.

06:44.349 --> 06:46.340
- Well, I'll have time.
- Ooh.

06:46.518 --> 06:49.009
Hey, 97, that ought to lift your spirits.

06:49.187 --> 06:51.212
I'm ebullient.

06:52.924 --> 06:56.087
I feel like an idiot. I didn't know
you could make an appointment.

06:56.261 --> 06:58.525
Well, most people don't.

06:58.697 --> 07:00.255
Am I right?

07:03.234 --> 07:06.431
- Lena.
- Oh, I'm Alan.

07:06.604 --> 07:09.573
Ooh. You have a firm handshake, Alan.

07:09.741 --> 07:10.867
I like that in a man.

07:11.176 --> 07:14.668
Well, I'm a chiropractor.
My hands are my instruments.

07:14.846 --> 07:19.112
And I also carry a little squishy ball
in my pocket to head off carpal tunnel.

07:19.617 --> 07:21.107
Ooh.

07:24.456 --> 07:26.617
- How much can I bet?
- How much did you bring?

07:27.225 --> 07:28.783
I have to use my own money?

07:29.361 --> 07:31.829
Boy, you really are your father's son,
aren't you?

07:32.897 --> 07:34.296
Okay.

07:34.466 --> 07:36.661
I have $ 14.

07:36.835 --> 07:39.303
That's not gonna get you very far.

07:39.604 --> 07:43.199
Oh, and I have
a $50 gift certificate to Pizza Hut.

07:43.408 --> 07:46.502
- Wanna buy it?
- Sure. I'll give you 25 bucks.

07:46.678 --> 07:47.804
But it's won'th 50.

07:47.979 --> 07:50.140
- To who?
- To Pizza Hut.

07:50.315 --> 07:53.512
Well, then let the good folks
at Pizza Hut place a bet for you.

07:53.918 --> 07:55.510
You're just trying to rip me off.

07:55.687 --> 07:58.178
I've been staying up nights
trying to figure out...

07:58.356 --> 08:00.916
...how to get my hands
on your pizza money.

08:01.726 --> 08:03.216
Now listen and learn.

08:03.395 --> 08:07.161
In any financial transaction, there is one
question both parties ask themselves.

08:07.332 --> 08:09.425
We're going to a party?

08:09.801 --> 08:11.098
Will you shut up and listen?

08:11.269 --> 08:13.032
I thought we were going to the track.

08:13.671 --> 08:16.868
I swear to God,
I will throw you out of this car.

08:17.509 --> 08:19.170
Now, as I was saying.

08:19.477 --> 08:23.174
The question is, what leverage do I have
in this transaction?

08:23.348 --> 08:25.111
And the answer for you is none.

08:27.252 --> 08:28.719
What's leverage?

08:28.887 --> 08:30.821
Oh, boy.

08:31.289 --> 08:34.087
All right, a lever is how you move things.

08:34.259 --> 08:36.454
Leverage is how you move people.

08:36.628 --> 08:38.459
Now, if we were going to Pizza Hut...

08:38.630 --> 08:41.224
...and they didn't take real money
and I was starving to death...

08:41.399 --> 08:44.232
...your gift certificate
would give you leverage over me.

08:45.336 --> 08:47.361
But, alas, this is not the case.

08:48.640 --> 08:50.904
Okay, I guess I'll take $40.

08:51.076 --> 08:53.544
Now you're catching on. But no.

08:55.747 --> 08:57.908
&lt;i>WoMAN
Number 40 at Window E.&lt;/i>

08:58.083 --> 09:01.416
I'm sorry, baby. Mama's gotta stay here
till she gets her license.

09:01.853 --> 09:04.686
I'm hungry too.
I don't know how much longer.

09:04.856 --> 09:06.756
You wanna come in here
and wait with me?

09:06.925 --> 09:10.122
All right, you stay in the car
and play your video game.

09:10.295 --> 09:12.354
Mama loves you too.

09:13.064 --> 09:15.862
I get such little time with him.

09:16.801 --> 09:18.428
Where's his dad?

09:18.603 --> 09:20.093
Damned if I know.

09:20.271 --> 09:23.240
&lt;i>Now serving Number 41 at Window B.&lt;/i>

09:23.408 --> 09:27.777
Oh, he is gonna miss his piano lesson.

09:30.915 --> 09:33.577
Listen, why don't you take my number?

09:33.751 --> 09:35.514
- Oh, I couldn't.
- No, no, no, I insist.

09:35.687 --> 09:38.815
I've got somebody taking care
of my little boy, so I can wait.

09:39.624 --> 09:41.353
That is so sweet.

09:41.526 --> 09:44.222
&lt;i>Now serving Number 42 at Window B.&lt;/i>

09:44.395 --> 09:45.657
Oh, you're up.

09:45.830 --> 09:48.094
- Thank you so much.
- Oh, it's my pleasure.

09:48.266 --> 09:50.325
Hey, listen, maybe,
you think some time...

09:50.502 --> 09:52.197
...we could go out?
Hey, Mama.

09:53.771 --> 09:55.762
Baby, I thought you were
waiting in the car.

09:56.307 --> 09:59.174
- My batteries are dead.
- That's okay, we're out of here.

09:59.344 --> 10:02.438
- Wha...? You lied to me.
- No, I didn't.

10:02.614 --> 10:05.105
- Baby, you got a piano lesson today?
- Yup.

10:05.283 --> 10:06.910
Gershwin.

10:07.619 --> 10:09.177
See?

10:13.625 --> 10:17.322
Hey, I thought you had her
at "squishy ball. "

10:24.302 --> 10:26.167
So how much do I get if my horse wins?

10:26.337 --> 10:29.204
You bet 14 at 2-to-1, you win $28.

10:29.474 --> 10:30.998
That doesn't sound like a lot.

10:31.176 --> 10:33.041
Why can't I bet the 80-to-1 horse?

10:33.211 --> 10:35.702
You can but there's dogs
with forks and napkins...

10:35.880 --> 10:38.007
...waiting at the finish line
for that horse.

10:38.183 --> 10:40.981
- What's that mean?
- It means the greater the odds...

10:41.152 --> 10:42.346
...the lousier the horse.

10:42.520 --> 10:44.249
But he could still win, right?

10:44.422 --> 10:48.222
Yeah, and you could
still be class valedictorian.

10:48.393 --> 10:50.384
But that's not
where the smart money goes.

10:50.562 --> 10:53.156
You can make your point
without being mean.

10:53.331 --> 10:56.823
Look, if you want me to bet
the 80-to-1 horse for you, I will.

10:57.001 --> 10:59.526
- Okay, fine.
- It'll be a good lesson for you.

10:59.704 --> 11:01.865
You won't be such a know-it-all
when I win...

11:02.040 --> 11:05.009
Four times eight is 32.
One times zero is zero.

11:05.176 --> 11:07.576
- $ 120,000.

11:07.745 --> 11:09.337
All right, two lessons.

11:13.184 --> 11:16.347
It's not as much as I thought,
but I'm still rich.

11:17.155 --> 11:19.020
You're not rich...

11:19.190 --> 11:21.021
...you lucky little pecker-head.

11:22.026 --> 11:24.517
Hey, there's no reason for name-calling...

11:26.197 --> 11:27.789
...Mr. Smart-Money.

11:29.000 --> 11:30.058
You wanna walk home?

11:30.435 --> 11:31.800
I don't have to walk home.

11:31.970 --> 11:34.598
I could take a taxi or a limo.

11:34.772 --> 11:35.932
Or a hearse.

11:42.714 --> 11:44.011
Mmm.

11:44.182 --> 11:46.878
You were so smart to bring this.

11:47.719 --> 11:50.813
&lt;i>WoMAN
Now serving Number 97 at Window A.&lt;/i>

11:51.189 --> 11:53.657
Hey, that's me.

11:55.393 --> 11:57.554
You hang in there. Thanks for everything.

11:58.229 --> 11:59.560
You're welcome.

11:59.731 --> 12:01.722
I was being facetious.

12:10.241 --> 12:12.835
Ooh. Ninety-nine.

12:13.011 --> 12:14.638
Lucky you.

12:15.113 --> 12:17.206
I'm 138.

12:18.283 --> 12:20.217
Been here all day...

12:21.419 --> 12:23.387
...with my kid waiting in the car.

12:23.755 --> 12:25.382
Nice try.

12:30.795 --> 12:34.356
- Hey, Dad, guess what.
- Whoa, whoa, he doesn't need to know.

12:34.832 --> 12:36.732
- Why not?
- Think about it.

12:36.901 --> 12:39.802
What's your father gonna do
when he finds out you got $ 1120?

12:40.138 --> 12:42.698
Don't worry, I'm not gonna lend him any.

12:43.975 --> 12:45.101
No, you clod.

12:45.276 --> 12:48.143
- He's gonna make you put it in the bank.
- Oh, yeah.

12:48.313 --> 12:50.781
He's gonna give me grief
for taking you to the track.

12:50.948 --> 12:53.644
Oh, so I guess that means
I've got leverage on you.

12:55.753 --> 12:58.779
Hey, I can live with the grief.
Can you live without the money?

12:58.956 --> 13:00.856
No. I love my money.

13:01.292 --> 13:05.058
Okay, so here's what you do. Hide it
in your room someplace no one will look.

13:05.229 --> 13:09.825
I saw this movie where they put the money
in a plastic bag and hung it in the toilet.

13:10.001 --> 13:13.402
Bad idea.
Your toilet sees way too much action.

13:14.872 --> 13:16.601
Okay, I'll buy a big safe.

13:16.774 --> 13:19.072
Oh, brilliant,
that won't raise any questions.

13:19.243 --> 13:20.972
Just stick it in a shoe.

13:21.579 --> 13:23.843
But what if I wanna wear it?

13:25.750 --> 13:27.308
Then put it in a different shoe.

13:28.419 --> 13:30.887
But not the same pair, right?

13:32.657 --> 13:34.682
Correct.

13:35.126 --> 13:38.789
You have to be careful spending it.
You don't wanna call attention to yourself.

13:38.963 --> 13:40.692
Okay. I'll just get a plasma Tv.

13:40.865 --> 13:42.628
No, no, no.

13:42.800 --> 13:46.065
No plasma Tvs, no computers,
no expensive video games.

13:46.237 --> 13:48.102
Buy small stuff that no one will notice.

13:48.439 --> 13:50.464
- Like doughnuts?
- Okay. Perfect.

13:50.641 --> 13:52.472
What about a doughnut machine?

13:53.344 --> 13:54.868
Okay, you're not hearing me.

13:55.146 --> 13:56.545
I could hide it in the safe.

13:58.282 --> 14:00.079
Get out of here.

14:01.252 --> 14:03.686
Hey, where have you been?

14:03.855 --> 14:05.618
I told you. The DMv.

14:05.790 --> 14:08.122
All day? You should have
made an appointment.

14:10.128 --> 14:12.289
Yeah. Next time I'll know.

14:13.364 --> 14:15.355
So, what did you guys do today?

14:15.533 --> 14:18.627
Oh, not much.
We just hung out, ran a few errands.

14:18.803 --> 14:21.328
- Did you help him with his book report?
- Yes, I did.

14:21.506 --> 14:22.768
Really?

14:22.940 --> 14:24.567
No.

14:25.176 --> 14:27.167
- You said you'd help him.
- Yeah, you said...

14:27.345 --> 14:29.973
...you'd only be living here
for a couple of weeks.

14:30.615 --> 14:32.480
And you werert drunk when you said it.

14:32.817 --> 14:35.547
Fair enough. So you guys
just ran errands all day?

14:35.920 --> 14:37.478
Yes, errands.

14:37.655 --> 14:40.089
- Where is he, in his room?
- Yes, his room.

14:41.292 --> 14:44.022
- Thanks for keeping an eye on him.
- No problem.

14:46.130 --> 14:49.065
Oh, I have a bad feeling.

14:51.135 --> 14:53.865
Hey, Jake, I'm back. I was thinking...

15:00.511 --> 15:03.275
Uncle Charlie made me go to the track.

15:08.953 --> 15:10.011
What a day.

15:10.188 --> 15:12.679
Just sitting and sitting and sitting.

15:13.224 --> 15:14.555
Huh.

15:18.596 --> 15:19.824
It was like jury duty...

15:19.997 --> 15:22.830
...without the fun
of sending someone to jail.

15:23.734 --> 15:24.928
Sounds awful.

15:25.102 --> 15:26.967
Yeah, yeah.

15:27.638 --> 15:29.367
So...

15:30.441 --> 15:32.204
...you guys ran errands today.

15:33.678 --> 15:36.306
Little rat bastard sold me out, didn't he?

15:37.081 --> 15:39.242
Almost immediately.

15:40.084 --> 15:43.053
Why would you take a 13-year-old boy
to the track?

15:43.588 --> 15:47.388
Hey, I thought it would be better than him
hanging around the house doing nothing.

15:47.558 --> 15:49.753
He was supposed to be
doing his book report.

15:49.927 --> 15:51.554
Oh, yeah.

15:51.863 --> 15:55.959
And werert you supposed to be working on
some big credit-card jingle?

15:56.400 --> 15:57.890
I'm percolating.

15:58.603 --> 16:00.571
Boy, you are some role model.

16:00.738 --> 16:02.501
Well, one of us has to be.

16:03.875 --> 16:06.605
So exactly how much did he win?

16:06.944 --> 16:08.172
Eleven hundred dollars.

16:09.280 --> 16:10.304
Wow.

16:10.815 --> 16:13.181
Forget it. He's not gonna loan you any.

16:13.885 --> 16:17.252
All right, we'll put it in the bank.
A nice addition to his college fund.

16:17.588 --> 16:18.748
What college fund?

16:18.923 --> 16:21.448
The one with $ 1100 in it.

16:21.893 --> 16:23.087
Come on, Alan.

16:23.261 --> 16:25.593
He won the money fair and stupid.

16:25.763 --> 16:28.926
- So I ought to let him keep it?
- What's the worst that could happen?

16:29.100 --> 16:30.124
So he blows it.

16:30.301 --> 16:33.532
It's a life lesson
and we get a doughnut machine.

16:34.205 --> 16:35.297
What?

16:36.207 --> 16:39.370
- It's just money, Alan.
- Well, I don't want him to think like that.

16:39.544 --> 16:42.012
Oh, much better he think like you?

16:42.179 --> 16:44.647
Squirreling away every dime
so he'll have it handy...

16:44.815 --> 16:47.113
...for alimony payments and phone sex?

16:49.387 --> 16:52.049
For the last time, I misdialed.

16:52.957 --> 16:56.449
Yeah, every Wednesday night
for 20 minutes.

16:57.061 --> 16:59.325
Okay, we are not talking
about the phone bills.

16:59.497 --> 17:02.364
We are talking about teaching Jake
sound financial principles.

17:02.533 --> 17:04.865
And I am entitled to a date night.

17:06.504 --> 17:08.199
Fine, take the money away from him.

17:08.372 --> 17:11.239
- No, I'm not gonna be the bad guy.
- I'm not gonna be, either.

17:11.409 --> 17:14.242
- Why not? It's your fault.
- Lf you wanna point the finger...

17:14.412 --> 17:17.973
...look for the horse trainer who put
crystal meth in Mr. McGlue's feedbag.

17:20.217 --> 17:22.708
I'll bet that Clydesdale is still running.

17:23.321 --> 17:26.552
Okay, okay, you think you know him best?
We'll let him keep the money.

17:26.724 --> 17:29.557
But mark my words.
No good can come from a boy like Jake...

17:29.727 --> 17:33.663
...having that cash to throw around.
- Oh, come on, the kid might surprise you.

17:35.566 --> 17:37.830
- Here's a hundred bucks.
- What's that for?

17:38.035 --> 17:39.502
I broke a lamp.

17:47.945 --> 17:51.381
&lt;i>It's the card that's accepted
All over the globe&lt;/i>

17:51.916 --> 17:54.510
&lt;i>Something, something&lt;/i>

17:55.319 --> 17:58.117
&lt;i>Terry-cloth robe&lt;/i>

18:00.257 --> 18:02.282
That's enough for today.

18:02.660 --> 18:03.854
Hey, have you seen Jake?

18:04.028 --> 18:07.020
Oh, Little Lord Fartleroy?

18:07.698 --> 18:09.962
He wasrt pleased with grilled cheese
for lunch...

18:10.134 --> 18:13.535
...so he walked to Red Lobster
for their all-you-can-eat popcorn shrimp.

18:14.038 --> 18:16.370
- Wonderful.
- He lined his pockets with foil...

18:16.540 --> 18:18.371
...before he left.

18:19.010 --> 18:20.102
You think this is funny?

18:20.544 --> 18:22.375
So the kid gets to throw money around.

18:22.546 --> 18:23.911
- What's wrong with that?
Hey.

18:24.081 --> 18:26.914
Richie Rich back with my crab legs yet?

18:27.084 --> 18:28.813
No.

18:28.986 --> 18:32.387
You don't understand.
Money gives him choices and freedom.

18:32.556 --> 18:34.786
- Yeah, so?
- I don't have choices and freedom...

18:34.959 --> 18:37.427
...why should he?
- Dad, Uncle Charlie.

18:37.595 --> 18:39.927
Come out and see what I just bought.

18:40.831 --> 18:43.561
Oh, I have another bad feeling.

18:47.304 --> 18:50.398
Oh... Jake, where did you get that?

18:50.574 --> 18:54.567
A guy had it in the back of his pickup truck
at the gas station. It had a "for sale" sign.

18:54.745 --> 18:55.905
Oh, no.

18:56.080 --> 18:58.913
I asked him how much it was
and he said, "How much you got?"

18:59.083 --> 19:02.849
And I told him $ 1106 and he said,
"It's your lucky day. "

19:04.021 --> 19:07.286
Can you believe that?
That's two lucky days in a row.

19:10.428 --> 19:12.760
Okay, I'm sorry.

19:13.831 --> 19:16.322
- You did not ride that thing here?
- No, I pushed it.

19:16.500 --> 19:18.832
- I can ride it on the beach.
- You figured wrong.

19:19.003 --> 19:21.369
- It's too dangerous.
- Don't worry, I got a helmet.

19:23.107 --> 19:25.632
I traded him for a bag of crab legs.

19:27.445 --> 19:30.380
- Can you help me take it to the beach?
- You're not riding that.

19:30.715 --> 19:34.014
Well, I bought it with my own money,
so you can't tell me what to do.

19:37.555 --> 19:40.615
Really, I am as sorry
as I could possibly be.

19:40.791 --> 19:44.750
Let me show you how cool it is.
Look, the guy told me how to start it.

19:51.669 --> 19:53.796
He said it might need a tune-up.

19:56.540 --> 19:58.735
So where are my crab legs?

20:03.280 --> 20:04.372
Go ahead, say it.

20:04.548 --> 20:08.279
- I'm stupid and I got ripped off.
- No, no, nobody thinks that.

20:08.552 --> 20:10.543
I wouldn't say nobody.

20:11.255 --> 20:12.916
- Charlie.
- Come on.

20:13.090 --> 20:14.853
It's not the end of the world.

20:15.025 --> 20:18.426
Look, Jake, sooner or later,
every guy gets hustled.

20:19.130 --> 20:20.688
- Even you?
- Even me.

20:20.998 --> 20:22.898
I remember when I wasrt
much older than you...

20:23.067 --> 20:25.433
...I spent 100 bucks on a bag of oregano.

20:29.507 --> 20:32.772
- Oregano?
- Your uncle was making spaghetti sauce.

20:33.210 --> 20:35.075
Yeah, in a parked car...

20:35.246 --> 20:38.306
...before I went
to the Pink Floyd Laserium show.

20:38.482 --> 20:39.574
Thank you.

20:39.750 --> 20:43.880
The important thing is you learn something
that will serve you for the rest of your life.

20:44.054 --> 20:46.955
- What's that?
- Always buy motorbikes and oregano...

20:47.124 --> 20:49.058
...from authorized dealers.

20:49.794 --> 20:51.659
No. No. That is not the lesson.

20:51.829 --> 20:54.662
- A fool and his money are soon parted?
- No.

20:54.932 --> 20:56.797
- Don't run with scissors?
- Do you mind?

20:56.967 --> 20:59.834
Go ahead.
I'm down to "don't eat the yellow snow. "

21:00.504 --> 21:01.994
That's not it, is it?

21:03.574 --> 21:07.032
No, the lesson here is that when
a little extra money comes our way...

21:07.211 --> 21:09.577
...we do the smart thing,
we put it in the bank.

21:09.747 --> 21:12.079
It makes reasonable interest
at minimal risk.

21:12.249 --> 21:14.217
And then we have it for a rainy day.

21:14.385 --> 21:16.319
- Do you understand?
- Yeah.

21:16.487 --> 21:17.784
Attaboy.

21:17.955 --> 21:19.786
Trust me, there is no better feeling...

21:19.957 --> 21:22.926
...than knowing you have a little nest egg
to fall back on.

21:26.163 --> 21:29.223
There are at least eight better feelings.

21:29.400 --> 21:32.130
Charlie!
- Coming.
